-- An EITHER input. JSONDECODE and a request decode it with the typed decoder,
-- which did not have a case for a type of two type arguments: it fell back to
-- the untyped decode, which gives NOTHING for an object and passes a string or
-- a number through as itself, so the rule below ran on a value of the wrong
-- type and the row came back "status":"success" (smucclaw/l4-ide#1084).

@export default Which side of an EITHER
GIVEN e IS AN EITHER STRING NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE side e IS
  CONSIDER e
    WHEN LEFT message THEN "left"
    WHEN RIGHT amount THEN "right"

#EVAL side (LEFT "no")
#EVAL side (RIGHT 5)
